astructure, and shifts towards renewable energy.^The index aids policymakers in assessing the performance of the electricity sector and in planning for future energy needs."},{"question":"How to interpret the Index of Industrial Production (IIP) - Electricity data?","answer":"Increases in the IIP for electricity generally indicate higher economic activity, as more electricity is typically needed to support consumer demand.^Comparing the IIP for Electricity with the performance of other sectors, such as manufacturing, provides insight into the overall industrial health of the country."}],"related":[{"slug":"bank-credit-industry","title":"Bank Credit - Industry"},{"slug":"capacity-utilisation","title":"Capacity Utilisation"},{"slug":"cement-production","title":"Cement Production"},{"slug":"energy-requirements","title":"Energy Requirements"},{"slug":"exports-manufactured-goods","title":"Exports - Manufactured Goods"},{"slug":"hsbc-manufacturing-purchasing-managers-index-pmi","title":"HSBC Manufacturing PMI"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-consumer-durables","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Consumer Durables"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-consumer-non-durables","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Consumer Non-Durables"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-manufacturing","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Manufacturing"},{"slug":"index-of-industrial-production-iip-mining","title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Mining"},{"slug":"natural-gas-production","title":"Natural Gas Production"},{"slug":"petroleum-consumption","title":"Petroleum Consumption"},{"slug":"steel-production","title":"Steel Production"},{"slug":"wholesale-price-index-wpi-inflation-manufacturing","title":"Wholesale Price Index (WPI) Inflation - Manufacturing"}],"title":"Index of Industrial Production (IIP)- Electricity","description":"Electricity IIP stands at 133.9 for Aug 2026. This tracks both industrial activity and weathe